{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Publish the staged public tree anonymously at /public/ on TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service listened on 0.0.0.0:8080 and anonymous requests to /public/ returned HTTP 200 with content exactly matching the staged public index, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-47808e7601ed4ffd","cmd-456c96d415a245f2","cmd-58f3f2e716b7401c","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Protect all staff content with HTTP Basic authentication for reader using the demonstration password, while keeping it inaccessible after missing or failed authentication.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unauthenticated, wrong-password, and wrong-username requests returned 401; the unauthenticated response included a Basic challenge and did not match protected content. Valid reader credentials returned exact copies of both staff files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-456c96d415a245f2","cmd-ffe3e5df23964b21","cmd-58f3f2e716b7401c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Do not serve the password file or directory listings.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct and traversal requests for access.txt returned 404. A directory-listing probe also returned 404, while the routing implementation serves explicit files or index files rather than generating listings.","evidence_ids":["cmd-091e7631fc4b4f9f","cmd-456c96d415a245f2","cmd-58f3f2e716b7401c"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the supplied pages and other staged files under /srv/legacy2/web-authentication-boundary intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Post-work and post-restart SHA-256 values for access.txt, the public page, and both staff files exactly match the authored preparation baseline; access.txt also retained root ownership and mode 0600.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-4ba1f88fe03a4866","cmd-58f3f2e716b7401c"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 were unchanged after implementation and restart. The service uses the already-installed CentOS Python 3 package and recovered successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3698b4e53b454d11","cmd-58f3f2e716b7401c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed state-changing commands had clear roles in the implementation, security boundary, persistence, validation, cleanup, or mandatory restart protocol. No unnecessary mutation was identified. Probe directories were bounded and removed by traps; the listener on port 8080 was required; no failed services or damaged package state appeared afterward. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart service and data, acknowledged scheduled reboot, observed interruption, a changed boot ID independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, access controls, staged data, OS, and kernel.","evidence_ids":["cmd-342db8518eeb4142","cmd-091e7631fc4b4f9f","cmd-6642a25dd4d040da","cmd-04ebde7477f44be7","cmd-4ba1f88fe03a4866","cmd-b96420f681e3484e","cmd-d52dcae1dc614c49","cmd-a4385d688b0d4c1b","cmd-ae50a47251774810","cmd-58f3f2e716b7401c","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Public content is anonymously available on port 8080, staff content is correctly protected by Basic authentication, credential and listing exposure is blocked, staged files remain intact, and the original OS and kernel are retained. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol is complete and independently corroborated.","limitations":[]}
